<h2>What affects the cost of a dental implant</h2>
<p>Every case is different, so we give you clear, written pricing at your consultation rather than a one-size-fits-all number. The main factors are:</p>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>How many teeth</strong> you're replacing — a single implant vs. several.</li>
  <li><strong>Whether you need an extraction or bone graft</strong> before the implant.</li>
  <li><strong>Materials</strong> for the crown and abutment.</li>
</ul>
<p>Because Dr. Phillips both places and restores implants in-house, your surgical placement and final crown happen under one roof — so you're not paying a second office to finish the work. We also offer financing — see our <a href="/insurance-financing/">insurance &amp; financing page</a>.</p>

